  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply by $\\frac{2}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $2$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/4ae0539ec4de70987e49105ca4284f2cabf6c55109613ecea38705e19e05d2b7.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{8}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{8}{15}.\n$$",
